tests/isla/traces.sh traces UDIV from armv9p4-udiv.ir, which this diff makes from armv9p4.ir, the
Armv9.4-A snapshot of the Sail model (isla-snapshots d8b31014).  The function
execute_aarch64_instrs_integer_arithmetic_div, which UDIV shares with SDIV, reads operand1 from
X[n] and operand2 from X[m], and for a nonzero operand2 it computes the quotient as
RoundTowardsZero(to_real(asl_Int(operand1)) / to_real(asl_Int(operand2))), where
RoundTowardsZero(r) is ceil(r) for r < 0 and floor(r) otherwise.  Isla implements no real-number
primitive.  The edit computes the quotient as tdiv_int(asl_Int(operand1), asl_Int(operand2)),
which Isla evaluates with i128::wrapping_div on concrete operands and with bvsdiv over 128 bits on
symbolic ones.

A trace from the edited IR describes the unedited model under two readings: that the edit
divides the same integers in the same order and leaves the function otherwise unchanged, and that
for integers a and b with b ≠ 0, a/b rounded toward zero equals tdiv_int(a, b).  Rust's i128::wrapping_div and
SMT-LIB's bvsdiv both truncate toward zero, and neither overflows on operands below 2^64 in
magnitude.  The edit replaces seven statements by one, so the jump to the zero case and the goto
that skips it name the same statements as before at indices six lower.  Apply with
`cp armv9p4.ir armv9p4-udiv.ir && patch armv9p4-udiv.ir < armv9p4-udiv.diff`.

